(*"basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute_select"
A **description_attribute_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned a descriptive text.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_select"
A **generic_attribute_list_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned a generic attribute list.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_select"
A **generic_attribute_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned a generic attribute.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute_select"
An **id_attribute_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned an identifier.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute_select"
A **name_attribute_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned a name.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.role_select"
A **role_select** specifies those objects that may be assigned a role.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute"
An **aggregate_id_attribute** is used for the case where there is more than one product data element for a specific identifier.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add an aggregate id attribute to product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994 and ISO 10303-43:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute.attribute_value"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **identified_item**.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute.attribute_value.__note"
The context in which *attribute_value* is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or be default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute.identified_item"
the collection of items that are identified.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute"
A **description_attribute** is the assignment of a descriptive text string to product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add a description attribute to product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994, ISO 10303-43:1994, and ISO 10303-44:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.attribute_value"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **described_item**.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item"
the item that is described.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute"
A **generic_attribute** is the declaration of a named attribute as a text string to enable it to be associated with product data. This capability shall not be used to replace more specific assignment capabilities if both are available to a specified target.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute.__example"
A person entity data type instance is included in both <<express:basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_select,generic_attribute_select>> and <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute_select,name_attribute_select>>. The name attribute of person is provided for the name value.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute.__note"
This entity provides the capability to define a generic attribute associated with product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994, ISO 10303-43:1994, and ISO 10303-44:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute.attribute_name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> used to name the **generic_attribute**.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute.attribute_value"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **generic_attribute**.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_assignment"
A **generic_attribute_assignment** is the assignment of a generic attribute to element of product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_assignment.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add a generic attribute to product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994 and ISO 10303-43:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_assignment.attribute"
the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute,generic_attribute>> to be associated with the product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_assignment.item_with_attribute"
the item to which the attribute is assigned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment"
A **generic_attribute_list_assignment** is the assignment of a named list of generic attributes to element of product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment.__note"
This entity data type provides a capability to add a named list of generic attributes to certain product data entity data types using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994, ISO 10303-43:1994, and ISO 10303-44:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment.attribute_name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> used to name the list of generic attributes.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment.attributes"
the list of <<express:basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute,generic_attribute>>s that are assigned to the element of product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.generic_attribute_list_assignment.item_with_attribute"
the item to which the attributes are assigned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute"
An **id_attribute** is the assignment of an identifier to product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add an id attribute to product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994 and ISO 10303-43:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.attribute_value"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **identified_item**.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.attribute_value.__note"
The context in which *attribute_value* is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or be default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item"
the item that is identified.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute"
A **name_attribute** is the assignment of a label by which the product data is known.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add a name attribute to product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994 and ISO 10303-44:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.attribute_value"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **named_item** is known.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item"
the item to which the name is applied.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.object_role"
An **object_role** is a specification of a role for the association of management type data with other aspects of product data and a description of that role.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.object_role.__note"
This entity provides the capability to add a role attribute to an association of management type data with other aspects of product data using a method that is upwardly compatible with ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.object_role.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **object_role**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.object_role.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **object_role** is known.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.role_association"
A **role_association** is the assignment of an <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> to an association of management type data with other aspects of product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.role_association.__note"
This entity data type provides a capability to add a role attribute to certain entity data types that specify associations between product data and administrative or management data. Such entity data types are specified in the <<express:management_resources_schema,management_resources_schema>>.
*)

(*"basic_attribute_schema.role_association.item_with_role"
the item to which a role is assigned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.role_association.role"
the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the **role_association** with product data.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_description_value"
The **get_description_value** function accepts an object to which a descriptive text string may be assigned and returns this description if present.

If a <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>> references the object, the function will return the value of the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.attribute_value,attribute_value>> attribute of this <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>>. Otherwise, the indeterminate value will be returned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_description_value.obj"
(input) the object for which a <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> is determined. This is an input to the function.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_aggregate_id_value"
The **get_aggregate_id_value** function accepts an object to which an identifier may be assigned and returns this identifier if present.

If an <<express:basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute,aggregate_id_attribute>> references the object, the function will return the value of the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute.attribute_value,attribute_value>> attribute of this <<express:basic_attribute_schema.aggregate_id_attribute,aggregate_id_attribute>>. Otherwise, the indeterminate value will be returned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_aggregate_id_value.obj"
(input) the object for which an <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> is determined. This is an input to the function.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_id_value"
The **get_id_value** function accepts an object to which an identifier may be assigned and returns this identifier if present.

If an <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> references the object, the function will return the value of the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.attribute_value,attribute_value>> attribute of this <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>. Otherwise, the indeterminate value will be returned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_id_value.obj"
(input) the object for which an <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> is determined. This is an input to the function.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_name_value"
The **get_name_value** function accepts an object to which a label may be assigned and returns this label if present.

If a <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>> references the object, the function will return the value of the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.attribute_value,attribute_value>> attribute of this <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>>. Otherwise, the indeterminate value will be returned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_name_value.obj"
the object for which a <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> is determined. This is an input to the function.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_role"
The **get_role** function accepts an object to which a role may be assigned and returns this role if present.

If a <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association,role_association>> references the object, the function will return the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> of the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association.role,role>> attribute of this <<express:basic_attribute_schema.role_association,role_association>>. Otherwise, the indeterminate value will be returned.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.get_role.obj"
(input) the object for which an <<express:basic_attribute_schema.object_role,object_role>> is determined. This is an input to the function.
*)


(*"basic_attribute_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/fundamentals_of_product_description_and_support/resource.xml
*)
